    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T00:03:21Z",
    "body": "Cause found: this is a false positive in the pinning test, not a gouge. The offending move is a true G2 arc, from (-20, 15, 5) to (-15, 20, 5) about centre (-15, 15) at radius 5.000, so it is exactly R off the block corner the whole way round. The test (`whole_model_pocket::clears_around_the_part`) sampled every feed linearly between from and to, so it measured the arc's CHORD. The chord's 1/16 sample (-19.688, 15.312) stands 4.698 from the corner, which is the reported 0.30 mm. verify was right to read the path clean. Fix: the test samples arcs on the arc (`ArcMove::point_at`), and the pinning test is un-ignored and passes. Next I'll check the backstop the issue asks for: the same corner cut as a straight G1 chord (a real 0.30 mm intrusion) has to read a Gouge in verify. A test is being added for that.",
