    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T00:16:21Z",
    "body": "Fix staged in the agent worktree (not committed or pushed; main owns the commit).\n1. Generator: no defect. The corner is a true G2 at R 5.000 about (-15, 15). The pinning test sampled arcs along their chords; it now samples them on the arc (`ArcMove::point_at`). `a_whole_part_adaptive_keeps_the_full_tool_radius_off_the_part` is un-ignored and passes.\n2. Verifier: there was a real hole. Law (b) (`sim::verify::section::tangency`) read a straight move only at its `to`. So the arc's chord as a G1 (1.46 mm into the corner) and a G1 tangent to a 4.70 circle (0.30 mm in) both read clean, because both ends of each chord stand R off the part. In `Mode::Area` (the pocket family) every chord is now measured against every boundary edge by segment-to-segment distance (`laws::dist2_segs`). `Mode::Boundary` keeps its old law points, because Face rows cross the face's open edge by design. That gap is filed as #43.\nPinned by `whole_model_pocket::a_feed_chorded_across_the_parts_corner_reads_a_gouge`. That test passes the G2 at R and the generated path, and convicts the chord, the 0.30 tangent G1, and the generated path with its corner G2 swapped for its chord (at that exact move).\nGates green: app whole_model_pocket, verify, area_controls, operations, golden_cl, solid_law, blind_floor, real_tip_contour, posed_contact, post_not_judged; all camcraft-sim suites; motion adaptive_hsm plus 13 verify-using suites; clippy -D warnings on sim and app --tests.",
